# 20. IMPORTANT DEVELOPMENT INSTRUCTIONS

These instructions are mandatory.

1. Build a fully functional game, not merely a UI prototype.

2. Every visible button must have a working function.

3. Do not create fake multiplayer using local bots.

4. Do not simulate player synchronization locally.

5. Use real Supabase Realtime communication.

6. All players in one room must share the same game state.

7. Do not use paid dedicated game servers.

8. Ensure the project can be deployed using Vercel Hobby and Supabase Free within their applicable usage limits.

9. Do not expose service role keys.

10. Do not use placeholder functionality for core mechanics.

11. Prioritize working gameplay over unnecessary decorative features.

12. Use reusable components and maintainable architecture.

13. Handle loading states, errors, disconnected players, and reconnecting.

14. Test the game with at least two separate browser sessions.

15. Do not declare a feature complete before testing it.

16. Use proper TypeScript types.

17. Ensure that desktop and mobile controls both work.

18. All gameplay mechanics must be integrated, not implemented as disconnected demonstrations.

19. Use original or properly licensed pixel-art assets.

20. Do not silently remove requested features because they are difficult to implement. If a technical limitation occurs, explain it and propose a working alternative.

